  "planning_notes": [
    "Target board is arduino:avr:uno; wiring preserved exactly as stated: LDR->A0, button->D2, DHT11 data->D7, TM1637 CLK->D4 and DIO->D5, and Serial uses baud 9600 with framing=line_or_idle and idle_timeout_ms=20.",
    "Added required DHT validity input: declare a single dht_valid on the same physical pin D7 and sensor DHT11. Temperature/humidity and validity share the same acquisition pin and frame coherence; model must use validity false to handle invalid data without stopping unrelated devices.",
    "No explicit button polarity is provided; the digital_input model is true at D2 HIGH. If the real wiring is active-low, inversion must be handled in the SysML model (device request stays unchanged).",
    "TM1637 displays the currently selected page; the model maps which measurement is written to tm1637_number after each button press.",
    "Serial reporting cadence (every 2 seconds) and exception behavior (illumination low AND temperature high) are implemented in SysML using elapsed_ms; the device layer only provides ports."
  ],
